requests.text:
{
  "q0": "PhD B noted that the major component in the second waveform was actually the air conditioner, which introduced a significant noise at 5 Hz. He observed that this noise was not a good illustration of room reverberation but rather of room noise, and pointed out that it was inappropriate as an example because it wasn't reverberation but a known noise source. He also mentioned that the visual spectrogram differences, particularly in high frequencies, were noticeable and that the noise attenuated the high-frequency components in distant recordings.",
  "q1": "The discussion on Eurospeech covered the upcoming deadline in Denmark (Aalborg) on May 13th, with a special session on Aurora having an extended deadline. The group was working on experiments with meeting recorder digits and a paper for Eurospeech. They noted that the new filter with shorter delay hurt performance on the well-matched Italian case but didn't hurt on mismatched cases. The group also discussed the need for better visual demonstrations of reverberation on the web page, suggesting improvements like zooming into spectrograms or using spectral slices to highlight differences in speech and noise characteristics.",
  "q2": "The discussion on patterns of noise in the recordings highlighted that the air conditioner introduced a major 5 Hz noise component in the second waveform, which was not reverberation but room noise. This noise was a poor example of reverberation effects and was inappropriate as an illustration. PhD B observed that the high-frequency components were significantly attenuated in distant recordings, and the visual spectrograms clearly showed spectral effects from indirect energy. The group also discussed that spectral subtraction before on-line normalization increased noise variance and could be problematic, suggesting a need for better filtering or normalization methods.",
  "q3": "PhD F thought Eurospeech was an important opportunity, with the group working on experiments related to meeting recorder digits and a paper submission. He noted that the new filter with shorter delay hurt performance on the well-matched Italian case but had little effect on mismatched cases. He also mentioned that the group was collaborating with OGI on spectral subtraction and that they were evaluating the impact of different parameters and filters on recognition performance, particularly in noisy conditions."
}

